{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>לְמִשְׁמֶרֶת לְאוֹת</b> (as a keepsake for a sign): as a remembrance that I chose Aaron for the priesthood, and they will no longer murmur against the priesthood — this is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Numbers 17:25). But this staff is not a sign except concerning the tribe of Levi, that it was chosen from among the rest of the tribes, not concerning Aaron that the priesthood should be his. The correct interpretation is: לְמִשְׁמֶרֶת לְאוֹת — as a sign concerning the tribe of Levi in place of the firstborn, for the burning was a sign concerning the priesthood, and the blossoming concerning the Levitical service, as I explained (Ramban on Numbers 17:6). And this is the reason for \"the staff of Aaron for the house of Levi blossomed\" (Numbers 17:23) — for the entire house of Levi it blossomed, and on their merit. It is also possible that since it became known through the staff that HaShem does not desire the firstborn and He desires the tribe of Levi, the priesthood would belong to Aaron without murmuring, for he is the most honored in the tribe and the prince among them by the staff, and to him belongs the prerogative of princely rule over that tribe. But this is not correct in my eyes, for Gershon was the firstborn of Levi."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:06:37.088644260Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}